<DocsLayout
  title="Phase 2 — Context seeding"
  description="Where Think OS becomes actually useful. The agent drafts your HOT-tier files from your connected tools."
  current="phase-2"
>
  <p>
    After install and a restart, run <code>/thinkos-continue</code> in a fresh Claude
    Code session. The agent walks through, in order:
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>Welcome &amp; auth check</strong> — verifies any plugin connectors needing OAuth are authorized.</li>
    <li><strong>Import an existing vault</strong> (optional) — if you have a markdown vault from Obsidian or an older Think OS install, point at it. The agent maps filenames to Think OS slots and copies content over, marking those files as seeded.</li>
    <li><strong>File picker</strong> — choose which un-seeded files to populate next.</li>
    <li><strong>Per-file flow</strong> — chip-pick which connectors to read from, see the draft, approve / edit / regenerate. Nothing writes to the vault without your OK.</li>
    <li><strong>Automations offer</strong> — at the end, optionally set up scheduled triggers (Phase 3).</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Files seeded</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>05 Profile/Identity.md</code> — role, working style, comm preferences.</li>
    <li><code>02 Projects/Project Index.md</code> — your active and dormant projects.</li>
    <li><code>01 Now/Current Focus.md</code> — what this week is actually about.</li>
    <li><code>03 People/People.md</code> — frequent collaborators with context.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Full playbook</h2>
  <p>
    For the agent-facing playbook this flow follows, see
    <a href="https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os/blob/main/docs/phase-2-seeding-playbook.md">
      docs/phase-2-seeding-playbook.md
    </a>.
  </p>

  <p class="text-muted text-sm mt-12">
    Rendered docs coming soon. For now, the source files in the repo are authoritative.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
